# GPU EP Dev Workflow (Windows)

## Agent temp files

Use **`C:\Users\asparkhi\workspace\temp`** for agent-generated artifacts during debugging and fixes:

- Build logs (`gpu-ep-build.log`, MSBuild logs)
- VS installer scripts/logs (`temp/install-spectre.cmd`, `temp/install-vs-deps.cmd`, etc.)
- One-off repro scripts, captured command output

Do **not** scatter these in the repo root or `onnx-hipdnn-ep/` unless the user asks.

## Key paths

| Item | Path |
|------|------|
| Repo | `C:\Users\asparkhi\workspace\onnx-hipdnn-ep` |
| Build tree | `C:\Users\asparkhi\workspace\build\onnx-hipdnn-ep` |
| Install prefix | `C:\Users\asparkhi\workspace\local` |
| MSVC + Git Bash launcher | `C:\Users\asparkhi\workspace\gpu-ep-msvc-bash.cmd` |
| LIT suite dir (binary) | `C:\Users\asparkhi\workspace\build\onnx-hipdnn-ep\test\lit` |
| LIT sources | `onnx-hipdnn-ep\test\lit\` |

Launch dev shell: `cmd /c C:\Users\asparkhi\workspace\gpu-ep-msvc-bash.cmd`

**Open files from Git Bash:** use `copen file.mlir` (uses **cursor-server remote-cli** on Remote SSH, not desktop `code.cmd`). Launch bash **from a Cursor integrated terminal** so `VSCODE_IPC_HOOK_CLI` is set. With `CURSOR_LAYOUT=unifiedAgent`, the file opens in the **Editor** tab — switch away from Agent if you do not see it. Helpers: `~/.bashrc` → `bashrc-gpu-ep.sh`.

**Toolchain:** VS 2022 Build Tools 17.14 (MSVC 19.44), CMake 4.3+, Python 3.14, Git for Windows on PATH (before Cygwin Git).

## Build

```bash
export LOCAL_DIR=/c/Users/asparkhi/workspace/local
cd ~/workspace/onnx-hipdnn-ep
python build.py --install_dir "$LOCAL_DIR" --config RelWithDebInfo -j 8 \
  --cmake_extra_defines CMAKE_VS_WINDOWS_TARGET_PLATFORM_VERSION=10.0.22621.0
```

Skip tests: add `--skip_tests`. Configure only: `--skip_build`.

## LIT tests (hip-mlir-compiler)

**Preferred** — CMake target (builds tools if needed):

```bash
cmake --build /c/Users/asparkhi/workspace/build/onnx-hipdnn-ep \
  --config RelWithDebInfo --target check-hip-mlir-lit
```

**CTest:**

```bash
ctest --test-dir /c/Users/asparkhi/workspace/build/onnx-hipdnn-ep/test/lit \
  -C RelWithDebInfo -V
```

**Direct lit** (from build tree):

```bash
cd /c/Users/asparkhi/workspace/build/onnx-hipdnn-ep/test/lit
lit -sv --param=build_mode=RelWithDebInfo .
```

Single file or subset:

```bash
lit -sv --param=build_mode=RelWithDebInfo path/to/test.mlir
lit -sv -j 8 --param=build_mode=RelWithDebInfo Conversion/onnx-to-hip/
```

Prerequisites: `pip install lit`; match `--config` / `build_mode` to the built configuration (`RelWithDebInfo`).

## Windows build gotchas (seen on this machine)

- **MSB8040 Spectre:** MorphiZen needs MSVC Spectre libs — component `Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.14.44.17.14.x86.x64.Spectre`
- **stdalign.h:** use Windows SDK 10.0.22621+ (`CMAKE_VS_WINDOWS_TARGET_PLATFORM_VERSION=10.0.22621.0`)
- **atlbase.h:** LLVM DIA needs VC ATL component
- **MorphiZen version script:** MSBuild must see Git for Windows (`C:\Program Files\Git\cmd`), not Cygwin Git 2.21
